.TH SYS_PROC_PERS_NAME 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_pers_name \- resolve a personality ID to a name
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_pers_name(int " perso_id ", char *" buf ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_pers_name ()
attempts to translate a personality identifier (for example native, Linux,
FreeBSD compatibility IDs) into a textual name.
.PP
The current `lib/sys` implementation issues syscall number 360 directly.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, a negative value is returned by the current implementation.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOSYS
The syscall number is not currently wired in native dispatch.
.SH NOTES
This interface is currently wrapper-only and does not have a native syscall
number definition in `sys/arch/i386/syscall.h`.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_proc_info (2),
.BR uname (2),
.BR sysinfo (2)
